r the quadratic to have no real roots, we need:\n\n\\[\n16 - 4c < 0\n\\]\n\nSolving this inequality for \\( c \\):\n\n\\[\n16 < 4c \\implies 4 < c \\implies c > 4\n\\]\n\nThe smallest integer greater than 4 is 5. Therefore, the smallest integer value of \\( c \\) such that the function \\( f(x) = \\frac{2x^2 + x + 5}{x^2 + 4x + c} \\) has a domain of all real numbers is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{5}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:262"}
